From 661e1af6b6418ece2bf2b582ffe16747977593f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:52:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: outline overview cards and actions on white paper

Static outlined task menus (styling half of the former 0011-overview-ready-haptics-and-static-task-menus): EinkOverviewUi gives the app chip and task menus a white paper with a 1 px black outline, black text and icons, no elevation or shadow, and zero-duration open/close animators, under config_flatLauncherSurfaces.

Change-Id: I6020f1ccf9c898fe15c15c7056f4a7352ade0822

The app chip outline reuses one RectF instead of allocating one per draw.

Task menus: the edge is drawn as foreground above the options (which covered it), plain child fills are dropped so option selectors show, and the menu uses the overview ink, paper and outline width.
